# Class loading

## Three phases

- **Loading** — find + parse the bytes → a `Class` object
- **Linking** — **verify** bytecode, **prepare** statics, **resolve** references
- **Initialization** — run `static` blocks + static assignments

```java
class Config {
    static final int MAX = load();          // runs at INITIALIZATION
    static { System.out.println("init"); }  // ...on first use of Config
}
```

## The verifier — bytecode **proven safe** before it runs

No stack underflow, no bad jumps, no `int`-as-reference; hostile `.class` rejected at load time.

## Loader hierarchy

Parent-first delegation: **Bootstrap** (core JDK) → **Platform** (JDK modules) → **Application** (your classpath). A loader asks its **parent** first, so `java.lang.String` can't be counterfeited.

